THOUGHT: The field stringValue is documented as “May be null” and has no @Nullable annotation, so NullAway treats it as @NonNull. Other setters (double, String) also accept nullable stringValue and assign it directly, causing similar errors, but I must only fix the specific long setter. To satisfy NullAway without changing the public API, I can keep accepting a nullable parameter but store a non-null canonical representation when it’s null (e.g., String.valueOf(value)), mirroring the comment that null means “string representation is the string value of the long”. I’ll update only this method accordingly.

```bash
cd /home/vscode/nullness-benchmarks/libgdx && sed -i '1186,1190s/public void set(long value, @Nullable @Null String stringValue) {
    longValue = value;
    doubleValue = value;
    this.stringValue = stringValue;
    type = ValueType.longValue;
  }/public void set(long value, @Nullable @Null String stringValue) {
    longValue = value;
    doubleValue = value;
    this.stringValue = stringValue != null ? stringValue : String.valueOf(value);
    type = ValueType.longValue;
  }/' gdx/src/com/badlogic/gdx/utils/JsonValue.java && ./gradlew gdx:compileJava -x test -q > new_build_output.log 2>&1 || true && grep -n "JsonValue.java:1189" new_build_output.log || true && tail -n 40 new_build_output.log | grep -i "NullAway" || true```

